<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Brierley raises Hardie stake.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Brierley raises Hardie stake.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand-based Brierley Investments Ltd and its Australian offshoot Australian Consolidated Investments Ltd said they increased their holding in local building products firm James Hardie Industries Ltd by two percentage points to 27.23 percent.</p>
<p>Brierley was already the largest shareholder in James Hardie, which has recently sold some non-core assets in Australia and New Zealand.</p>
<p>It now has a holding of 106.952 million shares. James Hardie shares closed at A$3.35, unchanged on the day.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-29373-1800</p>
</text>
